acceptance_criteria:
- Frames {seq, samples[{containerId, cpu, memUsed, memLimit, netRx, netTx, blkRead, blkWrite}]}
- Worker stops on last UNSUBSCRIBE/disconnect, permission denial test
- Real STOMP test with mocked ContainerStatsService

- Unit/integration tests (Testcontainers, test-only capturing PasswordResetCodeSender) cover:
  - a valid code resets the password and the new password matches the stored hash;
  - the code is single use (a second confirm fails);
  - the code expires after the TTL (fixed/offset Clock);
  - after 5 wrong attempts even the correct code fails;
  - a new request invalidates the previous code;
  - an unknown username in request is a silent no-op and in confirm gives the same exception as a wrong code;
  - policy violations are reported and the code is not consumed;
  - passwordChangedAt is set (setup no longer required).
- The DB row holds only a 64-char hex hash, never the 6-digit code (asserted in a test).
- A log-capture test shows the code never appears in logs.
- ./backend/mvnw -f backend/pom.xml test passes.

- MockMvc + Testcontainers tests (capturing sender bean) cover:
  - request for an existing and a non-existing user both return 202 with identical bodies;
  - confirm with a valid code returns 204, after which login with the new password works and the old one fails;
  - wrong/expired/used code -> 400 INVALID_RESET_CODE;
  - policy violation -> 400 PASSWORD_POLICY with violations;
  - missing CSRF token -> 403;
  - blank fields -> 400;
  - both endpoints are reachable without a session.
- The request DTOs' toString doesn't contain the code or password (test).
- The CLAUDE.md Code Map entries for AuthController/SecurityConfig/auth dto are updated.
- ./backend/mvnw -f backend/pom.xml test passes.
